Subject: [PATCH] fix(display): let the backend decide backlight control by default

AppleARMBacklight impersonation with backlight-control published is what made
brightness work on 16.6.1, and this driver keeps that answer. On 27 the backend
owns the panel and the brightness scale, so publishing control from here as
well would give CoreBrightness two authorities over one panel.

The boot argument name does not change: `k60_backlight_control=1` still turns
the publication on, and the flag is still what the K60 BACKLIGHT evidence line
prints, so an image can be compared with the 16.6.1 ladder.

This is a behaviour change, not an optimisation. The same source publishes on
16 and does not on 27, so a `control=` field from one ladder cannot be compared
with the other; the saving of one boot argument is only a side effect.

Rationale and evidence: docs/research/display/DISPLAY-27-DELTA.md section 6.

Applies to the 27 ladder branch only. The closed 16.6.1 series keeps the
current default and must not take this patch.
---
--- a/drivers/PongAdreno/K60Backlight.cpp
+++ b/drivers/PongAdreno/K60Backlight.cpp
@@ -326,18 +326,23 @@
      * With the default, the service still publishes IODisplayParameters and
      * accepts brightness/FadePeriod requests, so a level can be driven from
      * either side, and nothing that walks the registry is told a backlight
      * control exists. */
-    /* backlight-control is the default since brightness-19 and 120hz-7: both
-     * published conformance=1 control=1 on the device with no SIGSEGV, the
-     * first frame presented and SpringBoard at 128-172 lines, and the user
-     * confirmed the slider range end to end (DBV 0x4 .. 0xfff). The earlier
-     * int-236 crash family came from publishCalibration() handing CoreBrightness
-     * a half-built dictionary, not from the impersonation itself, and that call
-     * no longer publishes the dictionary. Keep k60_backlight_control=0 as the
-     * explicit opt-out for an image that must not walk the registry with a
-     * backlight control published. */
-    uint32_t controlArg = 1;
+    /* On 16.6.1 backlight-control is published by default: brightness-19 and
+     * 120hz-7 both published conformance=1 control=1 on the device with no
+     * SIGSEGV, the first frame presented, SpringBoard at 128-172 lines and the
+     * slider range confirmed end to end (DBV 0x4 .. 0xfff). The int-236 crash
+     * family came from publishCalibration() handing CoreBrightness a half-built
+     * dictionary, not from the impersonation itself, and that call no longer
+     * publishes the dictionary.
+     *
+     * On 27 the decision belongs to the backend: the display driver owns the
+     * panel and the brightness scale there, so this driver keeps answering the
+     * conformance query and leaves control off unless the image asks for it
+     * with k60_backlight_control=1. This is a behaviour change, not an
+     * optimisation: the same code publishes on 16 and does not on 27, so a
+     * control= field from one version cannot be compared with the other. */
+    uint32_t controlArg = 0;
     const bool controlGiven = bootArg("k60_backlight_control", controlArg);
     if (controlGiven ? controlArg != 0 : true) {
         /* A successful vtable swap is not the answer that matters: brightness-4
          * swapped it and backboardd still crashed. The flag records the
